{
  "topic": "Why bees build hexagonal cells",
  "language": "en",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "Why are honeycombs hexagons? 🐝",
  "hook": "Why do bees build their honeycombs with perfect hexagons?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_hook",
      "narration": "Why do bees build their honeycombs with perfect hexagons?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why hexagons?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "hexagons?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_wax",
      "narration": "The wax comes from their own bodies, and it's expensive: about six to eight kilos of honey for every kilo of wax.",
      "on_screen_text": "Wax is expensive",
      "highlight_words": [
        "expensive"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_circles",
      "narration": "If they used circles, there would be gaps between the cells: wasted space and wax.",
      "on_screen_text": "Circles leave gaps",
      "highlight_words": [
        "gaps"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_shapes",
      "narration": "Only three identical shapes cover a flat surface with no gaps: triangles, squares and hexagons.",
      "on_screen_text": "Only 3 shapes fit",
      "highlight_words": [
        "3"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_less",
      "narration": "And of the three, the hexagon needs the least border to enclose the same area.",
      "on_screen_text": "The hexagon uses less",
      "highlight_words": [
        "less"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_proof",
      "narration": "Mathematicians suspected it for centuries, and in nineteen ninety-nine Thomas Hales proved it.",
      "on_screen_text": "Proved in 1999",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1999"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_double",
      "narration": "Plus, the comb has two layers of cells, back to back, sharing the walls at the bottom.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two layers in one",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Two"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_uses",
      "narration": "In those cells they store honey and also raise the baby bees.",
      "on_screen_text": "Pantry and nursery",
      "highlight_words": [
        "nursery"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_spoon",
      "narration": "And each worker bee makes just one twelfth of a teaspoon of honey in its whole life.",
      "on_screen_text": "1/12 of a teaspoon",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1/12"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
