  "description": "Wax comes from the bees' own bodies and costs a lot of honey. Only triangles, squares and hexagons tile a plane with no gaps, and the hexagon encloses the same area with the least border; Thomas Hales proved it in 1999 (the honeycomb conjecture). The comb has two layers of cells back to back, used for honey and for raising larvae. Each worker makes about 1/12 of a teaspoon of honey in its life. Original 3D animation.",
